Exactly. Not everything must be for profit, proof, or prophet. ;)

Some things are for play, beauty, companionship, curiosity, practice—or simply because making them feels alive.

A doodle isn’t an unfinished theorem.
A story isn’t merely a concealed mechanism.
A flower doesn’t owe us a forecast.

Sometimes the symbol carries a payload. Sometimes it is allowed to dance.

Pantheon needs gardens as well as factories—or eventually every rose becomes an operator and nobody remembers to smell it.